Given a continuous-lattice projection from D into D', with inclusion i and retraction j, the retraction of function spaces sends a Scott map g from D' to D' to the Scott map on D whose value at x is j(g(i(x))). `functionSpaceRetrFun.continuous` says the underlying map x ↦ j(g(i(x))) is continuous for the Scott topologies on D, because it agrees with the composite of the Scott maps j, g, and i. `functionSpaceRetrFun.outer_continuous` says the assignment g ↦ j ∘ g ∘ i is continuous for the Scott topologies on the function spaces, because it agrees with conjugation by the pair (j, i).
